\uline{Theorem 3} Let $X$ be a scheme of finite type over a field $K$, a finitely generated extension of $\mathbb Q$, we assume that $X$ is \deleted{\unsure{connected} smooth} \inserted{geometrically 0-connected,} and embeds in an extension of an abelian variety by a torus (for example $X$ is an elementary Artin variety, with typical fibres \inserted{fibres} distinct from the projective line and from the affine line).

\margin{it would suffice $K$ finitely generated over a prime field, not necessarily of characteristic 0 -- but in this form it is not very usable in characteristic $p>0$, see comments below...}

Consider \deleted{the map} \inserted{an} algebraic closure $\overline K/K$, and \deleted{\unsure{the}} the corresponding outer extension \inserted{$E_{X/K}$} of $E_{\overline K/K}=\operatorname{Gal}(\overline K/K)$ by $\pi_1(\overline X)$ $(\overline X=X\otimes_K\overline K)$, and the induced extension $\widetilde E_{X/K}$ of $E_{\overline K/K}$ by $\pi_1(\overline X)_{\mathrm{ab}}$. Consider the canonical maps
\diagram{\begin{tikzcd}[ampersand replacement=\&,column sep=large,row sep=large]
(*)\quad X(K) \arrow[r] \& {\begin{gathered}\text{classes of }\inserted{\pi(\overline X)\text{-}}\text{conjugacy of}\\\text{splittings of }E_{X/K}\text{ over }E_{\overline K/K}\end{gathered}} \arrow[d,dotted] \\
(**)\quad X(K) \arrow[r] \& {\begin{gathered}\text{conjugacy classes of splittings}\\\text{of the extension }\widetilde E_{X/K}\text{ of }E_{\overline K/K}\text{ by }H_1(Y).\end{gathered}}
\end{tikzcd}}
